summary: 'Built the consolidate forecaster (the N-branch generalization of weave''s 2-way forecast) and met Jinx''s falsifiable demand (T-2026-06-24-012): a contended same-feature fixture proving Warpline reduces HUMAN merge labor vs git, not the easy non-intersecting case. consolidate(refs[]) absorbs base+N refs in parallel (now safe per the just-shipped T-2026-06-23-003 fix), diffs each vs base, runs the proven 2-way predict pairwise, and aggregates by symbol into N-way knots/dangles/auto-folded. The fixture: 4 branches all edit one function''s return line — 2 alpha-equivalent renames (zero essence delta → auto-fold) + 2 divergent changes (one real knot). Measured K_human=1 < C_git=3: Warpline asks ONE decision where git''s sequential merge halts THREE times. The multi-agent thesis moves from asserted to SHOWN on contended work.'
